# e2e-testing (Cursor)

Patterns-only reference for writing good Playwright tests. No runner, no
report, no CI wiring of its own — when the task is "set up or run E2E for
a webapp," apply `webapp-testing` instead (it owns the standard runner and
report format and points back here for pattern choices). Scope is
browser-driven E2E only; pure API testing with no browser is `api-testing`.

## Data hygiene

A browser-driven test always creates data through a real running app —
there's no in-process transaction to roll back. Tag what a spec creates
and tear it down (automatic + a standalone script for crashed runs) rather
than letting it accumulate — see `api-testing`'s DB-strategy reference for
the approach. If a flow depends on an entity another repo/service owns,
stop and ask before seeding it directly.

## Organization and Page Object Model

Structure tests under `tests/e2e/<area>/*.spec.ts`, with `fixtures/` for
shared setup. Wrap each page's selectors and actions in a Page Object
class (`goto`, `search`, `getItemCount`, ...) rather than repeating raw
locators across tests.

## Test structure

`test.describe` per feature, `beforeEach` to construct the page object and
navigate, one behavior per `test()`. Assert on visible outcomes
(`expect(locator).toContainText(...)`), not internal state.

## Config essentials

`fullyParallel: true`, retries only in CI, `trace: 'on-first-retry'`,
`screenshot: 'only-on-failure'`, `video: 'retain-on-failure'` for a plain
Playwright setup (webapp-testing's own config differs — always/on for
report richness). Multiple browser projects (chromium/firefox/webkit) plus
a mobile viewport project as needed.

## Flaky-test handling

Prefer auto-waiting locators (`page.locator(...).click()`) over bare
`page.click()`; wait for a specific network response instead of
`waitForTimeout`; wait for element visibility/stability before interacting
during animations. Quarantine known-flaky tests with `test.fixme`/
`test.skip` referencing the tracking issue rather than leaving them
red/ignored. Identify flakiness with `--repeat-each=10`.

## Artifacts

Screenshots (`page.screenshot`), traces (`browser.startTracing`), video —
all should land under a consistent artifacts path so a failure report can
link back to them.
